Ah, I see it! You almost had it, but the detailLoading condition is still sitting inside the button's disabled property. That is what's causing the grey flash when you click the next arrow.
If you look around **line 546** in the code you just pasted, your button currently looks like this:
```javascript
            <Button
              variant="outlined"
              size="small"
              startIcon={<FileDownloadIcon />}
              onClick={handleDownloadExcel}
              
              disabled={detailLoading || !viewingBatchId} // <-- This detailLoading is causing the flash!
              sx={{ textTransform: "none", borderRadius: 1.5  }}
            >
              Export Excel
            </Button>

```
### The Fix:
Simply delete detailLoading || from that line. **Replace that whole <Button> block with this exact code:**
```javascript
            <Button
              variant="outlined"
              size="small"
              startIcon={<FileDownloadIcon />}
              onClick={handleDownloadExcel}
              disabled={!viewingBatchId} // <-- detailLoading is removed!
              sx={{ textTransform: "none", borderRadius: 1.5  }}
            >
              Export Excel
            </Button>

```
Once you remove that, the button will stay perfectly white and clickable while the table smoothly loads the next page!
